From 0938ad544ca0d509067cdf5e8975e9046597db1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:28:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Read pictures with Inkling 2: its mmproj on the CPU, GENI in
 its engine

Inkling 2's engine took text only (GEN / BGEN), and strata-vision
read Qwen's towers only. Now:

- the CPU tower (VitCpu) reads Inkling 2's (projector inkling2v, the
  type under clip.vision): a class token, the position table at its
  32 x 32 grid or bilinear (ggml's half-pixel centres), a pre-norm,
  separate q / k / v, the 2D rotary on pairs (a head's first half by
  the column + 1, its second by the row + 1, the class token at 0),
  layer scales, an erf GELU (a tier kernel: Abramowitz-Stegun, within
  1.5e-7), the patches merged 2 x 2 into mm.1, erf GELU, mm.2. The
  picture padded to a multiple of 40 (with -1 before the
  normalisation), resized only past 4,096 tokens, as mtmd. Against
  llama.cpp's mtmd at 640 x 640, 1000 x 700, 333 x 251 (padded) and
  4000 x 3000 (resized): every token's cosine >= 0.99994. The GPU
  tower stays Qwen's: a GPU reader refuses the file before READY and
  the server starts the CPU one;
- the engine takes GENI / BGENI (<max_new> [keys] <file> <ids>, the
  file strata-vision's records): each picture's rows its run of
  <|unused_200054|>, not RMS-normed (llama.cpp's inkling2 norms token
  rows only). Each row's id becomes one past the vocabulary, made
  from the picture's key (img_keys, else its rows' hash) and the row,
  so lanes, checkpoints and parked conversations, all matched by
  ids, tell pictures apart; lookup drafts and penalties skip them;
A follow-up turn on the same picture reuses its state (270 of 282
tokens); another picture with the same grid reuses none.
